11 — Architecture direction
Architecture should support the project without turning it into an unnecessarily complicated enterprise system.
11.1 Proposed technology stack
Layer	Proposed technology
Frontend	React
Language	TypeScript
Build tooling	Vite
Styling	Tailwind CSS
UI primitives	A reusable component library or carefully built custom components
Icons	Lucide
Charts	Recharts
Backend	Node.js
API	Express
Database	PostgreSQL
ORM	Prisma or Drizzle, to be decided
Authentication	Firebase Authentication
AI	Gemini API
AI tools	Backend-controlled tool calling
Validation	Zod
Testing	Vitest + integration testing
Version control	Git + GitHub
Deployment	To be selected after architecture and environment testing

This is the proposed stack, not a requirement that Google AI Studio must generate every technology exactly as listed. We will verify what AI Studio supports smoothly and preserve architectural control.
Why this stack?
- React helps us build reusable interfaces.
- TypeScript improves correctness and understanding of data.
- Node.js allows us to build the API.
- PostgreSQL gives us relational data modeling.
- Gemini handles the AI capabilities.
- Firebase Authentication can simplify identity management.
- Zod helps validate API inputs.
