12 — Database blueprint
The database is the foundation of PLAN and LIVE. THINK will later consume this data through controlled services.

We should design the database around meaningful relationships rather than creating isolated tables for each screen.
12.1 Core entities
Initial entity inventory
Entity	Responsibility
Users	User account and profile
Tasks	Tasks, deadlines and status
Task Subtasks	Smaller steps within tasks
Task Recurrence	Recurrence configuration
Projects	Project organization
Project Milestones	Project progress markers
Goals	Long-term objectives
Goal Milestones	Progress milestones
Calendar Events	Events and scheduled activities
Habits	Habit definitions
Habit Schedules	Frequency and schedule configuration
Habit Logs	Daily habit completion records
Workout Sessions	Fitness session history
Exercises	Exercise definitions / session exercises
Exercise Sets	Set-level workout data
Routines	Routine definitions
Routine Steps	Ordered routine actions
Routine Logs	Routine completion history
Notifications	Notification records
AI Conversations	AI conversation history
AI Messages	Individual messages
AI Action Records	Proposed and executed AI actions

This is a logical entity inventory, not a commitment to 20 separate tables in the initial implementation. We will validate each entity and relationship during schema design.
