How we will work inside AI Studio
Rule 1 — Never give it the entire project at once
We will give it controlled tasks.

Bad:
Build my complete productivity application with habits, goals, AI, fitness, calendar, analytics, authentication and everything else.

Better:
Implement the application shell with the approved design tokens, sidebar navigation, responsive layout and reusable UI components. Do not implement backend functionality yet. Follow the provided product blueprint.

Then we verify it before proceeding.
Rule 2 — Every prompt has a specific scope
Every implementation prompt will include:
1. What we are implementing.
2. Existing architecture.
3. Requirements.
4. Constraints.
5. What must not be changed.
6. Acceptance criteria.
7. Testing requirements.
Rule 3 — Understand what AI generates
Whenever it creates important code:
- Understand the file's responsibility.
- Understand how it connects to other files.
- Understand the API.
- Understand the database relationship.
- Understand the logic.
- Understand the error handling.
I will help you understand the generated code as we go.
Rule 4 — Maintain documentation
We should maintain these files from the beginning:
Document	Purpose
PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md	Product vision, scope and functionality
ARCHITECTURE.md	Technical architecture
DATABASE.md	Database schema and relationships
DESIGN_SYSTEM.md	UI tokens, components and styling
DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md	What we've implemented and learned
DECISIONS.md	Important architectural decisions
README.md	Project overview, setup and usage

Rule 5 — Git checkpoints
Before substantial changes:
- Commit the current working version.
- Implement the feature.
- Verify.
- Test.
- Commit again.
We should use GitHub as our recovery system and source of truth, not rely solely on AI Studio's chat history.
Rule 6 — AI Studio doesn't make architectural decisions automatically
AI Studio is our development tool, not our architect.

We will decide:
- The architecture.
- The database structure.
- The module boundaries.
- The business rules.
- The API design.
- The AI permissions.
AI Studio helps implement those decisions.

